# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Virtual environment — 469 MB, and machine-specific. Rebuilt from
# requirements.txt in about a minute. Never commit this.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.venv/
venv/
env/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Python bytecode and test caches
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Generated output. Every file here is reproducible from committed code plus
# committed data — `validate` regenerates the synthetic worlds, `run` rebuilds
# the report. Keeping them out means the repo carries sources, not artefacts.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
output/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# LLM response cache. Local, potentially large, and rebuildable (at cost).
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Secrets. The API key lives in the ALPHAVANTAGE_API_KEY environment variable
# and must never be written to a file in this repo — these patterns are a
# backstop, not the mechanism.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
*.key
secrets.*

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Temp files from the atomic parquet/json writes in scripts/ingest.py
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.tmp.parquet
*.tmp.json

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OS / editor cruft
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.vscode/
.idea/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NOT ignored, deliberately:
#
#   data/real/transcripts.parquet    14 MB, and five weeks of downloading at
#                                    25 requests/day. Losing it means starting
#                                    over. Committing it makes the collection
#                                    portable, backed up, and reproducible by
#                                    anyone reading the study.
#   data/real/ingest_state.json      lets the download resume on another
#                                    machine instead of re-fetching.
#   data/real/earnings_dates.json    report dates; expensive to re-fetch.
#   data/real/universe.csv           the point-in-time membership list.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
